# Exports are refreshed from n8n, not committed: they are large, they hold full node bodies, and
# a committed copy gets read as current long after it stopped being. See exports/README.md.
exports/*.json

# The same reasoning, and the rule above missed it. Pulling a single node body out of a deployed
# flow to diff it leaves a .js scratch file here, and `exports/*.json` does not match it - three
# of them (.cf.js, .fln.js, .flo.js, extracts of Capture Failure and Fail Loudly) sat untracked
# until a commit hook asked about them on 2026-08-24. A stale COPY OF ONE NODE is the same lie as
# a stale copy of the whole flow, only harder to spot, so nothing extracted from the instance is
# committed from this directory.
exports/*.js
exports/.*.js

# ...but these four are NOT exports. They are the coverage contracts, and a contract that lives
# only in a container is not a contract. Losing them loses the answer to "which flows must be
# audited" and "which flows did the skill build" - the two questions whose absence let five
# skill-built flows sit outside the compliance programme until 2026-08-23.
!exports/MANIFEST.json
!exports/instance-listing.json
!exports/instance-register.json
!exports/provenance-sweep.json
